 {"id":"fabro-adf7","title":"engine: failed orchestration runs lose their stage journals (no PR, checkpoint tip without hook output)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T12:17:11.776Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T12:17:11.776Z","description":"Conductor run 01M1RQGZYTPZH1RKRSTKXZZWN4 failed in the develop leg; its run branch (origin/fabro/run/<id>) does not contain .fabro/journal/<id>.jsonl — only journals inherited from the denkhaus HEAD it was cut from. Succeeded runs land their journals via the PR merge; PR-less (orchestration) runs and failed runs have no such path, so the control function cannot revise a failed pass's painpoints from durable state (events remain the only source). Fix direction: checkpoint/push the journal hook output on terminal failure too, or give PR-less runs a lightweight merge/record path for .fabro/journal. Basis: run 01M1RQGZYTPZH1RKRSTKXZZWN4, workflow version absent, commit 4c1ca7e0a.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-fe35","title":"cli: automations command group — fire/list/inspect scheduled runs from the terminal","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:12:41.697Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:12:41.697Z","description":"The UI and API can fire automation runs manually (POST /api/v1/automations/{id}/runs), the CLI cannot — the command list has no automations group at all. Wanted: `fabro automations list`, `fabro automations fire <id>` (optionally --trigger), `fabro automations show <id>` mirroring the API. Primary consumer: the agent control function and the operator firing conductor passes without the UI (observed 2026-09-05: manual conductor proof had to go through curl + auth token extraction). Small, well-defined; good develop-workflow delegation candidate. Basis: conductor cron setup session, commit context 51adfced3.","labels":["cli","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-54f0","title":"engine: no approval timeout — pending approval_required runs wait forever (zombie pending)","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:23:20.240Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:23:20.240Z","description":"Run approval (ApprovalMode::Prompt) has NO expiry: a run sitting in pending/approval_required waits indefinitely for approve/deny, survives server restarts (startup reconciliation covers Runnable, not pending-approval), and nothing ever cleans it up. Observed live 2026-09-05: conductor children created via fabro_run_create defaulted to approval_required; two pending children waited until a human noticed (and the conductor agent recreated one, causing parallel develops). Wanted: configurable approval TTL (default e.g. 24h) after which the run fails with reason approval_timeout, surfaced in the UI pending list; complements auto_approve for orchestration children (fix 7fda51235) as the cleanup backstop. Basis: conductor production pass 01M1S5D9XC, commit context 3479aa998.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
-{"id":"fabro-78ac","title":"engine: fabro_run_create swallows the created run id when start fails (partial success reported as total failure)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:25:09.559Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:25:09.559Z","description":"create_runs_with_options does create-then-start with ?-propagation: when create succeeds (201, run exists pending) but start_run fails (e.g. approval_required 409), the ENTIRE tool call returns an error and the created run id is discarded. The calling agent believes the create failed and reasonably retries — producing duplicate parallel children (observed in conductor pass 01M1S5D9XC: children 01M1S5MWDT swallowed + 01M1S5RTW8 retried 8s later; both approved by a human, serialization broken, manual cleanup). Fix: report partial success — return the created run with its state (e.g. 'created <id>, start blocked: approval_required') so callers can poll/approve instead of recreating. Complements auto_approve (7fda51235), the one-child prompt rule (3479aa998), and the approval-TTL seed fabro-54f0. Basis: run 01M1S5D9XC events 16:13:24/16:13:32, commit context 3479aa998.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
+{"id":"fabro-78ac","title":"engine: fabro_run_create swallows the created run id when start fails (partial success reported as total failure)","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:25:09.559Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:41:13.158Z","description":"create_runs_with_options does create-then-start with ?-propagation: when create succeeds (201, run exists pending) but start_run fails (e.g. approval_required 409), the ENTIRE tool call returns an error and the created run id is discarded. The calling agent believes the create failed and reasonably retries — producing duplicate parallel children (observed in conductor pass 01M1S5D9XC: children 01M1S5MWDT swallowed + 01M1S5RTW8 retried 8s later; both approved by a human, serialization broken, manual cleanup). Fix: report partial success — return the created run with its state (e.g. 'created <id>, start blocked: approval_required') so callers can poll/approve instead of recreating. Complements auto_approve (7fda51235), the one-child prompt rule (3479aa998), and the approval-TTL seed fabro-54f0. Basis: run 01M1S5D9XC events 16:13:24/16:13:32, commit context 3479aa998.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
